{
 "_note": "The two short Day 1 items 95% Group's weekly timing guide opens with: Identify Phoneme, two minutes, and Articulate Phoneme, three. Identify asks whether the lesson's sound is in a word and whereabouts, because a child who cannot hear /sh/ at the end of fish will not spell it there; the position is read off the grapheme reader rather than judged. Articulate asks what the mouth is doing, which is what separates the pairs children confuse -- f and v are the same mouth with the voice off and on. Consonants only: what the mouth does for a vowel is a matter of degree and not something a child can check, so vowel lessons get the identify half alone. Both are spoken, so what prints is a teacher's card. Generated by scripts/build-phoneme-intro.mjs; do not hand-edit.",
